AMDGPU: callees read implicit kernel arguments through the implicit-argument pointer

Generic (all pre-gfx9 targets with code object v5 or later; gfx803 is where it
was found and tested).

Verified on an RX 590 (gfx803) with clang built from ROCm llvm-project
rocm-6.4.4 (d366fa84) with this patch and 0002: the probes below, and
PyTorch rebuilt with it (24 of 24 mixed fp16/fp32 ops at three sizes
correct, against 24 faults with the shipped compiler; SDXL UNet output
bit-identical, same step time).

WHY
---
On gfx6-gfx8 a few values that gfx9 and newer read from hardware come from
the kernel's implicit arguments: the queue pointer the trap handler expects
in s[0:1] at s_trap, and the private and shared aperture bases needed to turn
a stack or LDS address into a generic pointer. loadImplicitKernelArgument
computes their address with lowerKernArgParameterPtr, which in a function
that is not a kernel has no kernel-argument pointer and returns the bare
offset. The callee then loads the queue pointer from address 0xc8 and the
apertures from 0xc0 and 0xc4:

  s_mov_b64 s[6:7], 0xc8
  s_load_dwordx2 s[0:1], s[6:7], 0x0
  s_trap 2

The kernel already passes the implicit-argument pointer to such a callee (in
s[8:9]; AMDGPUAttributor keeps it live for trap and llvm.amdgcn.implicitarg.ptr
users), and the llvm.amdgcn.implicitarg.ptr intrinsic already reads it there
in non-entry functions; only this lowering ignores it.

What breaks without the patch, on gfx803 with ROCm 6.4.4:
- A failed assert() (__assert_fail is not inlined) prints its message and
  then ends with "Memory access fault ... on address (nil)" instead of the
  trap report.
- PyTorch's mixed fp16/fp32 binary elementwise ops (torch.maximum, atan2,
  mse_loss, gelu_backward, ...) fault whenever the element count is not a
  multiple of 16384: the last, partial block runs a non-inlined
  elementwise_kernel_helper whose prologue makes a generic pointer to its
  stack from the private base read at 0xc0.
- Any non-inlined function that casts a stack or LDS address to a generic
  pointer faults.

To reproduce: a __attribute__((noinline)) device function that calls
__builtin_trap(), or that passes the address of a local array to another
non-inlined function; its assembly shows a scalar load from a constant base
(0xc0, 0xc4 or 0xc8) instead of from s[8:9].

WHAT
----
In loadImplicitKernelArgument, a non-entry function takes the base from its
IMPLICIT_ARG_PTR input and subtracts the FIRST_IMPLICIT offset (the offset
getImplicitParameterOffset adds is relative to the start of the kernel
arguments; a callee's explicit argument size is 0). Kernels are unchanged.
The GlobalISel path (AMDGPULegalizerInfo) has the same flaw and is not
changed here; HIP selects with SelectionDAG.

Measured with the patched clang (RX 590, stock HSA runtime):
- the callee emits `s_load_dwordx2 s[0:1], s[8:9], 0xc8` and
  `s_load_dword s4, s[8:9], 0xc4`; an unpatched build of the same source
  emits the null-base loads above;
- a non-inlined stack-pointer cast passes (it faults built with the shipped
  compiler and with the unpatched build);
- a failed assert() ends with HSA_STATUS_ERROR_EXCEPTION and no VM fault.
LDS casts in callees also need the M0 patch that follows this one.

diff --git a/llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/SIISelLowering.cpp b/llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/SIISelLowering.cpp
index a9c99751a..7069e1840 100644
--- a/llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/SIISelLowering.cpp
+++ b/llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/SIISelLowering.cpp
@@ -6884,8 +6884,28 @@ SDValue SITargetLowering::lowerTrapEndpgm(
 SDValue SITargetLowering::loadImplicitKernelArgument(SelectionDAG &DAG, MVT VT,
     const SDLoc &DL, Align Alignment, ImplicitParameter Param) const {
   MachineFunction &MF = DAG.getMachineFunction();
+  const SIMachineFunctionInfo *Info = MF.getInfo<SIMachineFunctionInfo>();
   uint64_t Offset = getImplicitParameterOffset(MF, Param);
-  SDValue Ptr = lowerKernArgParameterPtr(DAG, DL, DAG.getEntryNode(), Offset);
+  SDValue Ptr;
+  if (Info->isEntryFunction()) {
+    Ptr = lowerKernArgParameterPtr(DAG, DL, DAG.getEntryNode(), Offset);
+  } else {
+    // A callee has no kernarg segment pointer; lowerKernArgParameterPtr would
+    // return the bare offset, i.e. a load from a null base. The implicit
+    // arguments are reached through the incoming implicitarg_ptr, which
+    // AMDGPUAttributor keeps live for functions that trap or cast LDS/scratch
+    // to flat under code object v5.
+    MVT PtrVT = getPointerTy(DAG.getDataLayout(), AMDGPUAS::CONSTANT_ADDRESS);
+    SDValue ImplicitArgPtr = getPreloadedValue(
+        DAG, *Info, PtrVT, AMDGPUFunctionArgInfo::IMPLICIT_ARG_PTR);
+    // getImplicitParameterOffset is relative to the kernarg segment start;
+    // the callee's explicit kernarg size is 0, so FIRST_IMPLICIT is the
+    // bias that separates the two bases.
+    Ptr = DAG.getObjectPtrOffset(
+        DL, ImplicitArgPtr,
+        TypeSize::getFixed(Offset -
+                           getImplicitParameterOffset(MF, FIRST_IMPLICIT)));
+  }
   MachinePointerInfo PtrInfo(AMDGPUAS::CONSTANT_ADDRESS);
   return DAG.getLoad(VT, DL, DAG.getEntryNode(), Ptr, PtrInfo, Alignment,
                      MachineMemOperand::MODereferenceable |
